course: dictionary
lesson: 9718
title: Summer, a word with two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Summer has two main meanings. The first is the warmest season of the year, between spring and autumn (fall). The second is the long break from school in summer, which Americans call summer vacation. Read the words around summer to see which meaning is used.
explain: «On a summer evening a field can twinkle with fireflies.» Here summer is a time of year, and the words evening and twinkle tell you it is warm and the light is fading. Try your meaning in the sentence. A time of year fits, so that is the meaning.
explain: Context also shows how summer behaves. «The yellow was hidden under the green all summer» means the whole warm season, not one hot afternoon. Ask: what does summer have to fit here? Then check your meaning in the sentence.
fact: Summer is the warmest season of the year, between spring and autumn (fall).
fact: Summer holidays (US: summer vacation) are the long break from school in summer.
fact: In the Northern Hemisphere (UK, USA, Canada) summer is roughly June to August; in the Southern Hemisphere (Australia, New Zealand) it comes at the opposite time of year.
fact: Summer has the longest days because the Earth's axis is tilted; away from the equator, summer days are long and winter days are short.
fact: Even in summer, thunderstorm clouds reach so high that their tops are far below freezing.
exercise: «On a summer evening a field can twinkle with fireflies.» What is summer in this sentence? | A cold night in winter | *A time of year, the warm season | A kind of bug | A school holiday
exercise: «The yellow was hidden under the green all summer.» What does summer mean here? | A single hot afternoon | A type of tree | The school holidays | *The whole warm season
exercise: «Thunderstorm clouds reach so high that their tops are far below freezing, even in summer.» What does the word even suggest? | *Freezing can happen high up, even in the warmest season | Summer is always cold | Clouds are never high | Thunderstorms only happen in winter
test: Why do summer days last longer away from the equator? | Because the Sun moves faster in summer | Because clouds stop the night | *Because the Earth's axis is tilted | Because summer is the same everywhere
test: When it is summer in the UK, what season is it in Australia? | Spring | Autumn | Summer | *Winter
exam: Which two meanings does summer have in a dictionary? | *Warmest season of the year and the long school break | Cold season and winter break | A tree and a flower | A hot drink and a sun hat
